vpinos-core (1.1.10) trixie; urgency=medium

  * VPinOS Configuration has a Sound Output section: pick the sound
    device and its profile, and Save makes that the output everything
    plays through.
  * New Setup > Audio Setup in the menu lists every sound device's
    profiles, with the active one marked, and every output with its
    volume, with the default marked. The menu's Setup options after
    VPinOS Configuration each moved down one.
  * System Info has a Sound section with the same listing.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:44:24 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.9) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Every app now uses the same /etc/vpinos/hyprland.conf: the installer,
    VPXConfig and VPinOS Configuration included, not just VPinball and
    VPinFE. The monitor modes and Table/Backglass/DMD screens saved in
    VPinOS Configuration now apply to all of them. Their floating,
    windowed layout is now a mode inside hyprland.conf, and the separate
    hyprland-installer.conf is no longer shipped. Existing cabinets keep
    their current hyprland.conf, and keep using their old
    hyprland-installer.conf for those apps.
  * VPinOS Configuration opens on the Table screen. It used to open on
    whichever screen Hyprland numbered first.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:24:55 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.8) trixie; urgency=medium

  * VPinOS Configuration fills the whole screen. Its window was floating
    at the size Chrome remembered, which only used the middle of a
    rotated Table screen. It is now maximized once it opens.

