vpinos-core (1.1.7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * VPinOS Configuration opens already rotated when Table Screen Rotation
    is set. The reload it runs at startup was dropping the rotation, so it
    only came back after the next Save.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:56:45 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Table Screen Rotation no longer rotates VPinball or VPinFE, which
    rotate the playfield themselves. It now rotates every other app:
    VPinOS Configuration, VPXConfig, the installer, System Info, the
    WiVRn dashboard, Chrome and windowed apps.
  * The rotation is saved to the new /etc/vpinos/table-rotation.conf
    instead of hyprland.conf. vpinos-launch applies it before starting
    each app, and VPinOS Configuration applies it to its own screen
    straight away on Save. A rotation saved with 1.1.5 is moved over on
    the next Save.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:39:19 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Portrait mode for a Table screen mounted in portrait.
  * VPinOS Configuration: new Table Screen Rotation setting (Off,
    90° Left, 90° Right). It rotates only the monitor assigned the Table
    role, using Hyprland's monitor transform in hyprland.conf.
  * Setup menu: new Console Rotation option (Normal, 90 Left, 90 Right),
    now item 1, with the other Setup items moving down one. It rotates
    the text console through fbcon, applies straight away, and is
    re-applied at every boot by the new vpinos-console-rotation.service
    and after a GPU driver switch. The setting is stored in
    /etc/vpinos/console-rotation, with a passwordless sudoers rule
    scoped to the new root helper.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:50:24 -0500

