vpinos-core (1.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Main menu: System Info (Debug) moves into a new Tools submenu.
  * Tools > VPX Editor: launches the VPX table editor (amd64 only),
    offering to install it from the VPinOS apt repo on first use, with a
    passwordless sudoers rule scoped to the new install helper.
  * vpinos-launch: new "x11" client, like "installer" (Xwayland DISPLAY,
    windowed Hyprland config) but for any app that needs X11.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:59:31 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Depends on vpinos-platform and vpinos-kernel: the kernel and the
    NVIDIA driver (prebuilt modules) now come through apt too.
  * Update VPinOS runs two apt rounds (pins first, then kernel/driver) and
    allows the downgrades a deliberate driver rollback needs.

